      "tag": "nit",
      "description": "`safe()` runs `tr` under `LC_ALL=C`, so it now masks other worktrees' paths byte by byte: every byte of a non-ASCII character, and common path characters like `~ + @ , : =`, become `?`. A checkout under `/Users/José/...` or `/home/me/c++/...` (including the main checkout, seen from a worktree) prints as `Jos??` or `c??`, and the model may then try to `cd` into a path that does not exist. Consider saying in the comment that the masked path is display-only, or printing a stable label such as the `.worktrees/` basename.",
      "body": null,
      "suggestion": null
    },
